# The transitive normal-dependency closure of celestina-lock-verify (design
# §4.14): the output of
#   cargo tree -e normal --prefix none -p celestina-lock-verify
# reduced to crate names. A crate that arrives through a feature or a
# transitive edge fails tests/closure.rs. Task 4 adds the same list for the
# lock process in celestina-lock/tests/closure.allow (T-D1).
bitflags
celestina-lock-proto
celestina-lock-verify
cfg-if
libc
linux-raw-sys
nix
rustix
zeroize
